course: dictionary
lesson: 4983
title: Freedom and doing things yourself
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Independence is a noun. It means being free to do things for yourself, without needing help or being controlled by others. When you tie your own shoes, you are showing a little independence.
explain: The word can also describe a whole country. «The United States declared its independence in 1776.» Here independence means the country became free to rule itself, instead of being ruled by another country.
explain: Look at the words around independence to check its meaning. «India won independence in 1947 after a long movement.» Won tells you that people fought for it and gained it, so independence is a freedom that can be won.
fact: Independence means being free to do things for yourself, or a country being free to rule itself.
fact: Children gain independence as they grow, for example by walking to school or making their own snack.
fact: «Gain independence» and «declare independence» are common phrases.
fact: «Independence Day» celebrates a country's independence.
fact: «Ethiopia kept its independence through the colonial period» means it stayed free and was not ruled by another country.
exercise: «The United States declared its independence in 1776.» What does independence mean here? | A large, empty field | *The freedom to rule itself, not be ruled by another country | Being very tired after a long day
exercise: Which is an example of a child gaining independence? | *Making their own snack | Being carried everywhere by an adult | Sleeping all day long
exercise: Which phrase means a country becomes free? | *gain independence | lose your temper | break a promise
test: «Ethiopia kept its independence through the colonial period.» What does kept its independence mean? | *It stayed free and was not ruled by another country | It lost all its money | It moved its capital to a new city
test: Which is the best example of independence for a child of ten? | *Tying their own shoes without help | Asking an adult to do every task | Refusing to leave the bed all day
exam: Which best describes independence? | *Being free to do things for yourself | Being sad and alone | Being given everything you ask for | Being very hungry
